      text Getting started danger
      h1 Class-less version
      text Embrace minimalism with Pico’s .classless version, a semantic option for wild HTML purists who prefer a stripped-down approach.
    col
      text Content
      link "Semantic containers" /docs/classless
      link Usage /docs/classless#usage
      link "Custom root container" /docs/classless#root-container
    col
      text Pico provides a  version ().
      row
        text .classless
        link example https://x4qtf8.csb.app/
      text In this version, , , and  inside  act as  to define a centered or a fluid viewport.
      text <header>
      text <main>
      text <footer>
      text <body>
      link containers /docs/container
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/classless
        text /* Containers */ body > header, body > main, body > footer { ... }
      text These 2 pages have the same style:
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/classless
        text "<!-- With pico.min.css --> <body> <main class=\"container\"> <h1>Hello, world!</h1> </main> </body>"
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/classless
        text <!-- With pico.classless.min.css --> <body> <main> <h1>Hello, world!</h1> </main> </body>
      text See the  to easily select the ideal Pico CSS version variant to match your project's needs.
      link "version picker" /docs/version-picker
      h2 Usage#
      text Use the default .classless version if you need centered viewports:
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/classless
        text "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/pico.classless.min.css\">"
      text Or use the .fluid.classless version if you need a fluid container:
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/classless
        text "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/pico.fluid.classless.min.css\">"
      text These  versions are also available on :
      row
        text .classless
        link "jsDelivr CDN" https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@picocss/pico@2/
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/classless
        text "<!-- Centered viewport --> <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@picocss/pico@2/css/pico.classless.min.css\" >"
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/classless
        text "<!-- Fluid viewport --> <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@picocss/pico@2/css/pico.fluid.classless.min.css\" >"
      h2 Root container#
      text If you need to customize the default root container for <header>, <main>, and <footer>, you can recompile Pico with another CSS selector.
      text Useful for , , or .
      row
        link React https://reactjs.org/
        link Gatsby https://www.gatsbyjs.com/
        link Next.js https://nextjs.org/
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/classless
        text "/* Custom Class-less version for React */ @use \"pico\" with ( // Define the root element used to target <header>, <main>, <footer> // with $enable-semantic-container and $enable-responsive-spacings $semantic-root-element: \"#root\", // Enable <header>, <main>, <footer> inside $semantic-root-element as containers $enable-semantic-container: true, // Enable .classes $enable-classes: false )"
      text The code above will compile Pico with the containers defined like this:
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs/classless
        text /* Containers */ #root > header, #root > main, #root > footer { ... }
      text Learn more about .
      link "compiling a custom version of Pico with SASS" /docs/sass
      link "Edit this page on GitHub" https://github.com/picocss/picocss.com/blob/main/app/routes/docs.classless.jsx
